  "question": "Does one EOF data-page insertion with existing inline global/owned/available map capacity match DAO controls and subsequent insertion while preserving all unrelated original bytes and page0?",
  "sequence": [
    "Commit and independently review the finalized source/input pins before one acquisition, no retry or resume.",
    "Create three natural DAO schema/data profiles times three replicas, each with an unrelated table and KeepQuery. No raw fixture mutation: empty Items, Items with ten 180-byte payload rows, and similarly dense Later after Items. Retain closed originals; each DAO control is a separate original copy receiving the declared insertion once.",
    "Public Unix insert_row on a private original copy must return exactly EOF/slot 0 and append exactly 2048 bytes. Require preexisting inline maps to cover EOF, the original global bit to be free and both table bits clear. Dense source pages must naturally have insufficient room. Exact original prefix changes only the table count and those three map bits; the new page equals the declared checked Long/Long/Text row image. Page zero remains unchanged.",
    "Only all nine complete candidates permit read-only original/control/Rust observations plus separate DAO follow-on insertion copies of control/Rust. Full schemas, rows and KeepQuery SQL compare after both stages; physical DAO control placement need not equal Rust EOF placement. Retain 45 MDBs and 63 read captures.",
    "Any creation, eligibility, mutation, observation or preservation failure remains no_outcome; retain partial images and initiating errors. No same-plan retry or subset promotion."
  ],
  "decision_rule": "observed_accepted only when all nine exact candidates and subsequent DAO continuations match complete expected semantics, retained source/image/operation identities and exact EOF/map/count/prefix preservation. Existing-page allocation policy and unchanged page zero are tested candidate choices, not inferred DAO counter or threshold rules.",
  "bounds": "One new data page only, unindexed relationship-free non-Auto/LVAL Long/Long/Text tables; no global free-page reuse, map expansion, indirect map, wide-row inference or compaction. Existing diagnostic limits of 64 pages, 64 columns and 64 rows per page suffice. SSH 300 seconds per phase, Unix 120 seconds. Local development only, no hosted/support claim."
}
